# Semantic commits in English

Every commit subject is English and follows `type(scope): subject`. Never Portuguese. Never a free-form title.

```
# ❌ BAD
feat: persiste projetos via tRPC
Add i18next with English-first catalogs

# ✅ GOOD
feat(auth): add Better Auth with login and 2FA
fix(kanban): stack project detail in the mobile drawer
```

- **type:** `feat` `fix` `docs` `style` `refactor` `test` `chore` `merge`
- **scope** (required unless the change is repo-wide docs): `i18n` `ui` `auth` `login` `kanban` `audit` `filters` `contacts` `projects` `invoices` `tools` `dashboard` `finance` `settings` `nav` `api` `db` `secrets` `github` `shared` `marketing` `repo`
- **subject:** imperative, lowercase, no trailing period, ~72 characters
- One logical change per commit. Body (optional) is English too.
- Merge commits: `merge(scope): pull request #N` or `merge(scope): short reason`
